From: Seabraid <seabraid@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/16] N-card ladder M3, engine side: ownership map +
 promotion rungs behind --retier-promote, and fail-closed tier rounds

OwnershipMap (one map of who executes each expert, one epoch) with prepare/commit transitions through two live rungs
(card 1's slots, card 2 over the channel); serve loop calls it between windows only when --retier-promote is given on top of
--retier (both opt-in).  The existing --retier path gains fail-closed behaviour: a tier round that times out, tears a slot or
reports stale residency CLOSES the helper card for the session (its experts come from RAM / the drive), and a helper slot whose
copy did not finish is quarantined (holds() says no, never lent, never written again).  ownership_map_test (CPU) covers the map.
